            <ArticleTitle>[A man with 3 arms. Phantom limb perception in intramedullary ependymoma].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>548-51</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report the case of a patient who suffers from a supernumerary phantom limb after the resection of an intraspinal, growing ependymoma at the level of C1-C3. Various mechanisms which might have produced the phantom limb are discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
